## What the MIT licence covers

The MIT licence in `LICENSE` covers the work in this repository:

- the MCP server — `mcp/src/**` (TypeScript) and `mcp/python/**`
  (the stdlib-only fallback);
- the index builder and the library tooling — `mcp/build/**`,
  `.build_library.py`, `.build_guide.py`, `.gen_report.py`;
- the installers, the test suite and the documentation;
- the skills written for this library: `caveman-mode`, `humanizer`, `latex-doctor`, `research-partner`, `skill-creator-plus`, `skill-library-adder`.

`skill-creator-plus` is derived from Anthropic's `skill-creator`
(Apache-2.0), with additional references, scripts and an eval-review
viewer. Its upstream terms are noted here because they apply to the
part it derives from.

## What it does not cover

Every other skill and agent under `skills/` and `agents/` is third-
party work, redistributed under its own licence. Some are MIT, some
are Apache-2.0, one is CC-BY-4.0. The licence file for each one is
in the upstream project it came from, and the attribution is listed
in `CREDITS.md`.

## Entries that were left out

An entry is published only if its own licence permits redistribution.
Publishing material whose licence forbids it would grant rights the
author did not grant, so those entries are **not** in this repository.

| Reason | Count |
|---|---:|
| Published | 952 |
| Excluded — the licence does not permit redistribution | 136 |
| Excluded — the maintainer's own private project files | 2 |
| Excluded — test fixtures, not published content | 3 |

The excluded entries are not listed here by name, because naming them
would defeat the point of excluding them: they would still be
pointed at. The count is the honest disclosure — the excluded set is
regenerated by `mcp/build/provenance.py`, which resolves a licence
per entry from the container manifest, the nearest `LICENSE` file,
the installed package metadata, or the entry's own frontmatter, in
that order.

